     7	# EP budget: f_hid (5.4) ALWAYS takes INT IN + INT OUT. ECM notify INT IN + HID IN/OUT = 3 INT:
     8	#   ep3 (INT, patched), ep4 (INT), ep5out (bulk+INT, patched). Bulk: ep1 pair (ECM), ep2 pair (ADB).
     9	#   ACM cannot also fit, so KD's ttyGS0 is replaced by a PTY<->TCP bridge (/data/ttygs_tcp_bridge).
    10	#   Link order matters (configfs binds in link order): ECM, then HID, then ffs.adb.
    11	#
    12	# Safety (v3, per GPT-5.6 review 2026-10-18):
    13	#  - adbd is started BEFORE the UDC is bound (FunctionFS needs descriptors first, else -ENODEV).
    14	#  - HID report_length 9 (report ID 1 keyboard = 1 ID + 8 bytes; pointer = 1 + 5).
    15	#  - EXIT trap: on ANY failure it unbinds, unlinks and removes our functions, restores stock serial
    16	#    (/data/setusbconfig serial) and restarts KeyboardDevice.
    17	#  - Stale links in g1/configs/c.1 are removed before reuse.
    18	#  - KD is stopped via its procd service (no respawn race) and restarted at the end. setusbconfig is
    19	#    shadowed by a tmpfs no-op bind mount (gone at reboot), so KD's restart does not wipe the composite.
    20	#  - KD gets a filtered `dmesg` (PATH shim via bind-mounted appLunch.sh) so its USB-reset hack does not fire on
    21	#    f_hid's harmless -EOPNOTSUPP for SET_IDLE/SET_REPORT (root cause of the 3 s flapping, 2026-10-18 15:53).
    22	#  - v3.2 boot mode (--boot, run by boot-every/composite.sh in the watcher): no host confirmation; instead a
    23	#    detached flap monitor polls /sys/class/udc/<udc>/state and rolls back if the link drops >=5 times in 60 s.
    24	#    Any rollback (failure, flapping, --rollback) ends in stock ACM + KD + adb (mk20-add-adb.sh).
    25	#  - Addressing (1.1.0+): usb0 172.30.250.2/24 (Mac MK20 service manual 172.30.250.1/24) + alias 169.254.7.2/16;
    26	#    fixed MACs. mk20d passes the configured values; the defaults here only apply outside release mode.
    27	#  - It must NEVER run inside an adb shell (it kills adbd; adbd kills the session group). It queues itself to the watcher.
    28	set -u
    29	LOG=${MK20_GADGET_LOG:-/mnt/SDCARD/mk20/logs/gadget-ecm-hid.log}
